Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:30:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Limit /api to 10 requests per second per token

rateLimit() runs on every /api route. It keys callers by a SHA-256 of
their bearer token (else their IP), asks that caller's RateLimiter for a
token, and answers an empty bucket with 429
{ error: "rate_limited", retryAfter: 1 } and Retry-After: 1. It fails
open, with a logged error, when the binding is missing (pnpm dev, unit
tests) or the limiter can't be reached. Tests drive real RateLimiter
instances through a fake namespace on a test clock.
